Subject: [PATCH] mfd: tps65217: do not match nonexistent legacy child compatibles

The regulator binding describes regulators below the ti,tps65217 parent,
and the backlight binding describes a named backlight child without a
compatible property. Their drivers already look up these nodes through
the parent TPS device. Neither binding defines ti,tps65217-pmic or
ti,tps65217-bl.

Do not ask the MFD core to find those nonexistent compatible children.
This avoids its "Failed to locate of_node" warnings on BeagleBone Black
without inventing DT nodes or suppressing legitimate match failures.
Keep the charger and power-button compatible matches and resources.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Johan Overby <johan.overby@vxmt.com>

--- a/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/tps65217.c
@@ -80,11 +80,9 @@
 static struct mfd_cell tps65217s[] = {
 	{
 		.name = "tps65217-pmic",
-		.of_compatible = "ti,tps65217-pmic",
 	},
 	{
 		.name = "tps65217-bl",
-		.of_compatible = "ti,tps65217-bl",
 	},
 	{
 		.name = "tps65217-charger",
